<!--Post: 4921--><!--Time: 1106817191-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4921"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 1:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Call me crazy, but maybe BTK is tired of the WPD not releasing information.  Maybe he placed that brick on top of the box from keeping it the wind from blowing away the package. But maybe it is a connection between the brick thrown through the back door of one of the Park City women.  Maybe BTK thought if he not only got KAKE there first for photos, they would surely take photos of the brick.  Or maybe im just grabbin to far. <BR> <BR>wichitan<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4921-->
<!--Post: 4925--><!--Time: 1106824437-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4925"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 3:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Actually, your theory is being expounded by others - so you are thinking along popular lines. <BR> <BR>There will be a press conference today at 10am on the Wichita TV channels.  I will let you know if they mention a link. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4925-->
<!--Post: 4968--><!--Time: 1106842392-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4968"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 8:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, I just watched that news conference.  It is frustrating that they won&#39;t say more than they do.  At least we know they might have found the seventh sign.  &#42;Sigh&#42;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4968-->
<!--Post: 4976--><!--Time: 1106843425-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4976"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 8:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Until BTK provides intimate details that only the police know, he&#39;s murdered no one else, as far as I&#39;m concerned. I wouldn&#39;t place too much emphasis on a brick! BTK reads the papers and these boards, too. He knows there was a brick used in the area. <b>Until he provides the exacting, hidden details of any crime, don&#39;t give him credit. He&#39;s getting off on all this excitement over a brick.</b><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4976-->
<!--Post: 4978--><!--Time: 1106843548-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4978"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 8:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I thought the conference was a joke, too. <BR> <BR>Not a word about the relevance of the brick - or what was in the box.   <BR> <BR>They don&#39;t have a clue.  <BR> <BR>And they dont seem to want the public&#39;s help, now do they? <BR> <BR>After 30 years and the PD games still continue. <BR> <BR>BTK will never get caught until there is a major changing of the guard. <BR> <BR>Where the heck is Tom?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4978-->
<!--Post: 4981--><!--Time: 1106843763-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4981"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 8:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George - good point.  Yet, somehow the PD claims they &#34;know&#34; the package was from BTK. <BR> <BR>And they have the missing one. <BR> <BR>It is their secrecy that bugs me.  There is no reason for it.  After this long - their methods are failures - will it take another 30 years before they see that? <BR> <BR>Landwehr looked gaunt - harried, does he call the shot?  Or is he just carrying out someone else&#39;s orders? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4981-->
<!--Post: 4988--><!--Time: 1106844882-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4988"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 8:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippy - 100% agreed. <BR> <BR>All they do anymore is tie the latest communication with BTK after FBI analysis, and then re-ask for the public&#39;s help.  Seriously, <BR>how do they expect us to be of any significant help when they hand us a book, but won&#39;t let us read it! <BR> <BR>If I have someone in mind to give WPD info about, it would be easier to do so with the confidence that it will be taken seriously and as valid info.  Sometimes, the secrecy of the police can feed into conspiracy theories of the public, and keep tippers from disclosing that &#34;one little piece of information&#34; that bags a SK. <BR> <BR>Can someone remind me after 31 years, why the secrecy is beneficial to WPD?  I understand why a few details must be retained to keep false confessions from happening, but they act like this is G14 CLASSIFIED!  RANT...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4988-->
<!--Post: 4994--><!--Time: 1106846249-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4994"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bridgieb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bridgieb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 9:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippy- <BR>you stated &#34;they have the missing one&#34;.Was that said in the press conferance?I was under the impression that #7 was still missing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4994-->
<!--Post: 4997--><!--Time: 1106846775-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4997"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 9:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;Ahem.  Excuse me.  Yes yes ... excuse me.  Now see this?  This is an ordinary box of CEREAL.  That&#39;s right.  A box of cereal.  It had a brick on it. <BR> <BR>Oh and we&#39;re not even going to tell you what the 7th one was or what it contained! <BR> <BR>Now.  If you remember any information, or have any tips to tell us.  Please contact the WPD.  Remember.  A box of CEREAL.  Think back.  Has your father or mother bought a box of this cereal?  If so we&#39;ll come by and swab them! :D&#34; <BR> <BR>Damn it, I&#39;ve been polite enough to agree this WHOLE time to keep information from the public for the benefit of the case, but when they  ask for help from the public and not even give a CLUE about what&#39;s going on ... now they&#39;re blundering the case. <BR> <BR>I no longer take the WPD seriously.  Tom Voigt does a better job of informing the public of some clues that might lead to tips, while at the same time understanding that some information is important to keep secret.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4997-->
<!--Post: 4999--><!--Time: 1106847561-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4999"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 9:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Catcher, you live in the area and I respect your point of view, you obviously know whereof you speak. I like Tippy&#39;s post also. I understand what you&#39;re saying. I also would feel annoyed and, yes, even manipulated.  <BR> <BR>Tippy, I had the same idea. I can see BTK enclosing proof that the package was indeed dropped by he, and a little note warning the police that they&#39;d better only do such-and-such. Or did you mean WPD was following orders from the FBI? The latter scenario bothers me and I live nowhere near Wichita. I&#39;ve come to like the citizens of Wichita - and Kansas - over the months. You&#39;re square shooters and very decent people. I hope that the case is and always will be WPD&#39;s.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4999-->
<!--Post: 5000--><!--Time: 1106847760-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5000"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 9:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was writing my post and didn&#39;t see Verm_inve&#39;s words. Heck! Maybe you all are on to something. It certainly seems as though WPD has its hands tied for <i>some</i> reason. I wish I knew the reason.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5000-->
<!--Post: 5017--><!--Time: 1106849985-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5017"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 10:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t think WPD are that bad anymore.  Many of us are complaining about the lack of any useful information at that meeting too soon.  They&#39;ve had the evidence for ... what?   a day? <BR> <BR>Let them process it.  The police have done an okay job releasing information when necessary.  I just got tied up with the emotions of the case, mainly because everyone else is. <BR> <BR>Maybe there should be an &#34;hour wait&#34; thing with each post, too make sure people&#39;s emotions are in check ...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5017-->
<!--Post: 5018--><!--Time: 1106850111-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5018"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 10:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George - &#34;It certainly seems as though WPD has its hands tied for some reason.&#34; <BR> <BR>Very Freudian<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5018-->
<!--Post: 5019--><!--Time: 1106850269-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5019"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 10:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->As we don&#39;t know BTK&#39;s identity, emotion is all we have ;&#41;. Actually we have information, too, and sound thinkers. Every third person has a different idea so it&#39;ll be chaotic for a time.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5019-->
<!--Post: 5027--><!--Time: 1106853076-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5027"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 11:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->i watched the conference, and read the post @ <a href="http://www.kake.com" target=_top>www.kake.com</a> and they stated they had found both packages, and believe they came from BTK &#40;sure the name on the outside of the cereal box game tha one away&#41;, then turned them over to the FBI for authentication.  Around here there is a a saying to someone who is having a bad day &#34;who pissed in your post toasties.&#34;  Although I think the number 7 package was found directly inline with the fed ex letter and the number 8 package aka the ceral box.  I think the brick plays a sugnificant role in the number 8 packages for one reason.  BTK knows he can taunt the WPD, but now he is also taunting the public, due to there lack of information.  Clearly BTK wants WPD to share there finds, but it seem to me being a wichitan, that WPD dont dare want to gove him that satisfaction. <BR> <BR>wichitan<!--/Text--></td></tr>
