<!--Post: 5227--><!--Time: 1106956340-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5227"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 3:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This has gotten <i>way</i> off topic...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5227-->
<!--Post: 5230--><!--Time: 1106959054-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5230"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hbtcontrol<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hbtcontrol<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 4:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m guessing that the Post Toasties box is a clue that WPD completely understands - perhaps what BTK interrupted one of his victims eating.  If that happens to be one of the Park City women, then the brick is part of the clues he&#39;s left.   <BR> <BR>BTK is probably having more fun than ever watching WPD spin their wheels and the amateur sleuths going off the deep end.   <BR> <BR>I think WPD screwed up these cases big time over the years.  But they have help now, supposedly, so I&#39;m hopeful that will make the difference.   <BR> <BR>I think both the Post Toasties box and the brick are clues.  Eventually we will know.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5230-->
<!--Post: 5231--><!--Time: 1106959277-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5231"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 4:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe, after reading many posts from people who are actually here to catch BTK and not use multiple names to further past agendas, that the meaning of the brick was threefold: utilitarian, as OK Mike has mentioned the area is windy; it&#39;s also vintage BTK as he knows Davis and Hedge are high on the &#39;possible&#39; list and a nearby crime has a thrown brick aspect. If I can understand this, so can BTK. <BR> <BR>Finally, BTK, when making drops, is possibly afraid to enter Wichita. Recently, he used a high-crime area at 2:00 AM. This time, Park City. MB&#39;s like this one remind BTK he&#39;s being sought. After all, if a cop&#39;s light starts flashing for a minor problem with BTK&#39;s car, BTK will probably think the entire jig is up; it&#39;s doubtful he&#39;d think, &#34;Oh, I guess my tail light must be out, I&#39;ll just pull over.&#34; Rather, I think he&#39;d see the lights and panic. He may pull over and be able to act casually, but it would be enough to scare him out of ever driving into Wichita again. Oddly, it may be safer for BTK in Wichita during the day than at night.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5231-->
<!--Post: 5233--><!--Time: 1106960085-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5233"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dorothy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dorothy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 4:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->IMO, the brick has no significance.  I think BTK just used it to keep the cereal box from tipping over or blowing away. <BR> <BR>I also think the cereal box was a lame attempt at humor. <BR> <BR>I think he chose that out of the way spot, because he was chicken and feared that police might be monitoring or have cameras up in other locations. I don&#39;t believe it&#39;s related to any other victims. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5233-->
<!--Post: 5277--><!--Time: 1107020657-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5277"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 9:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dorothy thank you forbring it back to the brick.  I would agree with you last statement, in that it was alot safer to drop it off out in the country, although I also feel it was necessary seeing how it was in Park City, and he put a brick on top of the box.  Lets say for a minute here, the WPD got the package, are they gonna examine it?  Are they gonna share ANY information?  I dont think I need to waste my typing skills to give you that answer.  BUT maybe BTK is thinkin along those same lines, maybe he decided that he was tired of WPD giving up his trophies to the FBI, without publication and to the average Joe Public.  Now the public &#40;AKA you and I&#41; and every other chatter out there is starved for new information, that we keep complaining were not getting enough of.  BTK thinks to himself, I have no problem sharing my trophies with the police and taunting them, why not give average joe an eye shot or 2 of some of them.  I will write a letter to KAKE, which means they will go out and snap off as many photots as possible, and then call the WPD.  The WPD will then decided what photos they can publish.  Just a thought and not trying to pick on anyone in here,  BUT THIS FORUM IS FOR WHAT ABOUT THE BRICK ONLY. <BR> <BR>wichitan<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5277-->
<!--Post: 5324--><!--Time: 1107049494-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5324"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 5:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If I didn&#39;t want a box to blow away in the wind I wouldn&#39;t put a brick on top of it. A sudden gust could blow the box outward away from the brick causing the brick to fall and leaving the box free to be blown away by the next gust of wind. If I wanted to assure that the box wasn&#39;t going to blow away I would put the brick inside the box. Now it is wiegthing down the bottom of the box from inside the box and it isn&#39;t going anywhere without the brick going too. <BR> <BR>He could have tied the box with rope or duct tape to the post to keep it from blowing away. After all &#39;Bind&#39; is his first name isn&#39;t it? <BR> <BR>The brick has some significance to it. <BR>A brick used to break glass for entry? <BR>A brick as used in WSU&#39;s Plaza of Heroines to imortalize names inscribed there like Tina and Petra and PJ Wyatt? <BR>A brick as an occupational clue. Worked as a mason? <BR>A brick on top of a box with the letter T on the box circled. Brick T. Prick Tease. Motive is women victims were percieved to be prick teasers. <BR>Just a few things to think about before we dismiss the brick as a mere paperweight.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5324-->
<!--Post: 5330--><!--Time: 1107053642-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5330"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 6:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very nice johno, and whats more that is assuming the box had anything in it at all.  I feel it was a clue for the public, one they didnt have to wait for-&#40;FBI&#41;.  One we could all see from the get go.  For all the reasons johno stated. <BR> <BR>wichitan <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
