<!--Post: 5781--><!--Time: 1107368101-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5781"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 10:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I would like to add a couple more things I have noticed about the brick.  First, for a dirt road, the brick appeared to be very clean.  Second, as Johno stated it would have been better to put the brick inside the box-&#40;AKA due to the wind&#41;.  Third he mailed the letter to KAKE-&#40;AKA they will get there first and snap off photos&#41;.  Fourth, I haven&#39;t ever heard of someone in wichita, or from any other of the surounding areas, try to portray themselves as BTK, thus would&#39;nt the BTK on the box give that away.  Fifth, the B looks like a thirteen, with that....what do you think about this.... <BR> <BR>B=13 <BR>K=how many killed <BR>T=and tortured <BR> <BR>now, I&#39;m just grabbin, but isnt that all we are really left with?  <BR> <BR>wichitan<!--/Text--></td></tr>
